---
description: Only add comments when truly necessary.
alwaysApply: true
---

Only add code comments when they provide essential non-obvious information.

Avoid redundant comments that simply restate what the code does.

Good comments explain:
- Why a non-obvious approach was chosen
- Complex business logic or algorithms
- Important gotchas or edge cases
- References to external documentation or tickets

Bad comments (avoid):
- Restating obvious operations (e.g., "# Set the value to x")
- Describing what can be clearly understood from well-named variables/functions
- Commenting every single line or block
